/* window_face.c
 *
 * The letters the chat panel is written in.
 *
 * The screen this program runs under carries one font, six pixels wide
 * and thirteen tall, and refuses every larger size asked of it. These
 * shapes were taken once from Calibri at twenty two pixels and written
 * down here, so the panel reads the same on every machine without asking
 * any screen for a font it does not have.
 *
 * A shape is one bit per pixel, lowest bit leftmost, one number per row.
 * The advance is how far the pen moves after drawing it, which differs
 * from letter to letter because Calibri is not a fixed width face.
 *
 * Calibri belongs to Microsoft and ships with Windows. Anything meant to
 * be given away should use Carlito instead, which has the same widths and
 * is free to pass on. Regenerating from Carlito changes one word in
 * tools/make-face.ps1 and nothing else.
 */
